 actually  did some work which was associated with  global clusters and when you completed  your phd you then apply for these things  called postdocs which are like you know  three year fixed term  uh research positions  and you apply for a bunch of them  because actually you know  there's so people competing for them and  so you know you have to apply for loads  in the expectation of getting maybe one  or two offers um he offered me a job so  i applied for a postdoc with him to work  on hubble space telescope images of  globular clusters hubble space telescope  hadn't been launched at that point just  before the hst was launched and so it's  quite a cool kind of job i mean i would  get this hubble space telescope images  globular clusters and actually do some  analysis kind of along these lines and  he phoned me up so he phoned me up to  offer me the job and but he was clearly  quite embarrassed by the conversation  and it was because  he had some really strange there were  some strange rules associated with his  job which i think had been imposed by  his collaborators rather than him  and the rule was you i would be employed  to do these specific things with this  hubble space telescope data  if along the way while i was analyzing  that data i found anything else  i wouldn't be allowed to be an author on  any paper that came out of anything that  i sort of serendipitously discovered  along the line which is just a really  weird thing to do right you'd have  thought you know if somebody who's  working for you find something really  interesting in the data at the very  least there'd be an author on the paper  that described the interesting thing  they found but clearly this was some  rule they had in their collaboration  that actually people working on their  data were only working on the thing that  they were allowed to work on and  anything else they weren't allowed to be  involved with  um so he clearly he's phoned me up to  tell me this kind of expecting me when i  learned that to turn down the job which  i eventually did so i went somewhere  else instead  which is a shame because it had been a  great person to work with although  having said that of course then hubble  space telescope was launched and it  didn't work so actually i'd have spent a  lot of time trying to figure out how to  do things with the really dodgy images  that came out of hst when it was first  launched  if you'd like to learn a lot more about  globular clusters why not check out our  astronomy channel deep sky videos we've  been making films about all the objects  in the messier catalogue including but  not limited to  these globular clusters you're seeing on  screen at the moment there'll be a link  on screen and down in the video  description that's deep sky videos
 

